  "macroOverview": "Global equities absorbed the Moody's US Aa1 downgrade in two sessions and pivoted to NVDA's blowout Q1 FY2027 earnings (Data Center +92% YoY, $80B buyback, 25x dividend hike). US30 printed a new year high of 50,830 intraday Friday; NAS100 sits 197 points below its year high of 29,679. Eurozone Composite PMI collapsed to 47.5 (29-month low) on May 23 PMI Flash -- a genuine recession signal being overridden by global momentum. US Composite PMI stable at 51.7; Manufacturing 55.3 (strongest since May 2022). UK Composite PMI 48.5 (13-month low). Gold at 4,523 continues its controlled -19% correction from the 5,586 Iran-war ATH. AUDUSD failed the bearish call as USD weakness from Moody's provided unexpected AUD support. US markets closed Monday 26 May (Memorial Day); FOMC Minutes Tuesday 27 May is the week's key event.",
